We observe that a similar reasoning as in Theorem \ref{thm2} shows that for $H = (V,E)$ $d$-flat hypergraph, we have $|E| \leq 1 + \sum_{i = 0}^{d} \binom{n}{i}$. We note that the Sauer-Shelah Lemma \cite{Sa72} provides a weaker bound $|E| \leq \sum_{i = 0}^{d+1} \binom{n}{i}$, using the fact that $d$-flat hypergraphs have VC-dimension at most $d+1$.

