The exhaustive gate is still running; the expensive part is deliberately structure-aware—each guess already chooses one legal incident edge for every left vertex, so the reported density will not be inflated by malformed candidates. I’ll optimize that measurement if it exceeds a practical self-test runtime, without weakening the 200,000-sample requirement.
